WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.109 --> 00:00:14.049
Japan… a country that brags about two things:
The first one is their used underwear vending

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:17.770
machines (really you can find on the streets!)

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:21.900
The second one is their immigration rate,
which is, by far, the lowest in the developed

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:22.900
world.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.130
By comparison, in the United States, the foreign-born
population has risen to 14%.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.340
Canada and New Zealand have 20% and 25% respectively.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:36.870
While Japan has less than 2%.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:44.079
So, what’s the reason for this?

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:47.940
Well, that’s their restrictive immigration
system.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.960
This makes Japan something of a dream country
for politicians like Donald Trump or Marine

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:53.960
Le Pen.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:59.410
If there is a word to define the current political
debate, that word would be “IMMIGRATION”.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:02.989
In Europe, countries argue about what to do
with the refugees.

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:06.680
And it seems that politicians across the board
share the opinion that immigration is a problem

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:07.740
that needs to be stopped:

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.740
 

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.220
So then, Japan is the perfect example for
what it means to live in a country free of

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:37.220
immigrants.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:42.070
And now you might wonder What does this mean
for their economy?

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:45.700
Do they really save money because they don’t
have to spend anything on social policies

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.700
for immigrants?

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.869
Do Japanesse workers enjoy a better standard
of living because they don’t have to compete

00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:52.869
with foreign workforce?

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:58.200
Today on Visual Politik we will answer all
those questions.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.810
But before, we are going to have a look at
the specifics of their immigration law.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:08.629
ONE COUNTRY, ONE CULTURE, ONE RACE

00:02:08.629 --> 00:02:14.170
This statement was said by the man who was
the Prime Minister of Japan in the mid-1980s,

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.610
YASUHIRO NAKASONE.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.940
It clearly summarizes the immigration philosophy
of Japan.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:24.090
Basically, there are just two ways of getting
into the Land of the Rising Sun: one is with

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.230
a work contract, the other is with a tourist
visa.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.090
If a company wants to hire you overseas, you
will still need a visa.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:36.010
And the only way you get a visa is by having
a university degree or having some specific

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.840
skills that are practically impossible to
find in the Japanese labor market.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.670
So, if you are just a construction worker,
you’re never going to be able to get a work

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.120
permit…

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.790
That is unless you use this other program...

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:55.620
“Since Japan didn’t have a law to accept
workers from other Asian countries, like Vietnam

00:02:55.620 --> 00:03:00.830
or the Philipinnes, they created the so-called
TECHNICAL INTERNAL TRAINING PROGRAM”.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:05.819
This in summary is like becoming an Intern
in Japan… but getting half of the salary

00:03:05.819 --> 00:03:08.010
that a Japanese intern would get.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.800
Not only that, but with this “technical
internal training program”, your boss is

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:15.650
allowed to hold onto your passport and even
access to your bank account.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:24.300
More worryingly, since they started this program,
thousands of Asian immigrants have just disappeared.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:30.660
“When the Union representative spoke with
me, she said that my attitude was bad and

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:36.010
that If I continued to have this attitude…
if my actions continued, her friend would

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:39.620
hire a hitman to kill me”.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.959
So what if you enter with a tourist visa?

00:03:41.959 --> 00:03:46.360
Well, in that case, you can stay in the country
for a year and half as long as you can prove

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.280
you are studying Japanese.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.659
Once that time has passed, you need to be
hired by a company.

00:03:51.659 --> 00:03:53.700
And that can lead to a work visa.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.959
But watch out!

00:03:54.959 --> 00:04:01.000
Unlike other places like the US or the EU,
the Japanese working visa specifies your profession.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:06.569
This means if you have a work visa for being
a chef, you cannot work as anything other

00:04:06.569 --> 00:04:07.880
than a chef.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:12.230
If you break this rule, your work permit will
not be renewed.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:17.049
There is only one really effective way for
a foreigner to make a living in Japan:

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:21.789
“The easiest way to live here is by marrying
a japanese person”

00:04:21.789 --> 00:04:27.680
Now you can understand how it is possible
that a country with over 127 million inhabitants

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.539
has just 2 million immigrants.

00:04:30.539 --> 00:04:37.080
But what consequences does this have on the
daily life of of Japanese citizens?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:42.680
WHO PAYS JAPANESE PENSIONS?

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.300
Japan is the oldest country in the world.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.500
Not because of their long history but because
of the average age of their population.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:56.430
In fact, estimations say that in 90 years,
they will lose over 44 million inhabitants

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:00.490
(about the entire population of Canada) because
of this.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:04.259
This wouldn’t be a problem if it wasn’t
for the Social Security problem.

00:05:04.259 --> 00:05:10.289
As you know, the pension system in most of
the countries works this way: the people who

00:05:10.289 --> 00:05:14.800
are working today are the ones who pay the
pension of those who are retired.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:19.219
As the workforce gets smaller and smaller,
year after year, there are less and less people

00:05:19.219 --> 00:05:22.830
paying the pensions...

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:28.169
And more and more retired citizens needing
to draw social security.

00:05:28.169 --> 00:05:31.999
And this is why things like this happen:

00:05:31.999 --> 00:05:38.259
“Social security contributions cover only
60 per cent of these benefits.

00:05:38.259 --> 00:05:48.669
The remaining 40 trillion yen comes from taxes
or, more precisely, public deficits”.

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:50.999
By the way, this beautiful sound you are listening
to is the music of MESCALINA, a rock and roll

00:05:50.999 --> 00:05:53.129
band from Spain who sent us their music.

00:05:53.129 --> 00:05:55.580
If you like it, check the links on the description
box below.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:01.779
So even if the social security contributions
are increasing year after year, Japan cannot

00:06:01.779 --> 00:06:03.919
pay their pensions effectively.

00:06:03.919 --> 00:06:12.080
And this is why… and pay attention to this,
Japan has the highest public debt IN THE WORLD.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.539
Their debt is more than double their GDP.

00:06:15.539 --> 00:06:20.020
And their fiscal deficit (the difference between
their income and their spending) is higher

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.110
than the US one.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:26.990
In other words… if Angela Merkel goes there,
she is gonna get really angry!

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:30.189
Mow you might be wondering: What does this
have to do with immigration?

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.689
The answer is, well, A LOT.

00:06:32.689 --> 00:06:36.430
You see, we all have heard about how expensive
it is to integrate immigrants.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:42.770
You have to pay social programs, integration
courses, etc… but no one talks about how

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:46.379
much it costs for a normal, native citizen.

00:06:46.379 --> 00:06:52.729
For example, an American-born citizen costs
the government an average of $150,000 from

00:06:52.729 --> 00:06:58.699
birth until he or she is 16 years old - and
this is only education and healthcare.

00:06:58.699 --> 00:07:01.479
Depending on the state, you might add in other
spending.

00:07:01.479 --> 00:07:06.080
All this money the government views as an
investment - money the government will get

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.919
back the day that citizen starts working and
paying taxes.

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:12.389
On the other hand, let’s take the example
of a Vietnamese immigrant to Japan.

00:07:12.389 --> 00:07:15.330
He comes to the country when he is old enough
to start working.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:20.169
His education and healthcare was already paid
for by the Vietnamese government.

00:07:20.169 --> 00:07:26.169
In an average of two years, this immigrant
will find a job.

00:07:26.169 --> 00:07:29.949
Of course, it might be a low-paid one, and,
therefore, he will pay little tax.

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:33.719
But the Japanese government didn’t have
to invest almost any money into him.

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:37.159
So, in other words, immigrants are free cash
for the government.

00:07:37.159 --> 00:07:42.649
Since Japan has so few immigrants, they are
losing out on this influx of easy money.

00:07:42.649 --> 00:07:47.780
This is why, in the middle of a fiscal crisis
in the year 2015, the Japanese Premier, Shinzo

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:53.739
Abe, made this announcement.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:08:00.259
“Japan is under pressure to accept more
immigrants as the workforce shrinks”

00:08:00.259 --> 00:08:04.429
But, despite what it looks like, this is not
Japan’s biggest problem: Japan has seen

00:08:04.429 --> 00:08:08.719
20 years go past without any economic growth.

00:08:08.719 --> 00:08:10.969
This is what experts have called the “lost
decade”.

00:08:10.969 --> 00:08:16.409
And yes, immigration has a lot to do with
this as well.

00:08:16.409 --> 00:08:19.289
THE COUNTRY THAT STOPPED INNOVATING

00:08:19.289 --> 00:08:23.509
We all imagine Japan as the country of technology
and innovation.

00:08:23.509 --> 00:08:27.849
The country where companies like Nintendo,
Sony, and Toshiba were all born.

00:08:27.849 --> 00:08:34.250
Nonetheless, all these firms are very OLD!

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:36.810
Nintendo was founded in 1889.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.060
Toyota was created in 1937.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:40.060
Actually…

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:43.599
Can anybody name five Japanese companies created
in the 21st century?

00:08:43.599 --> 00:08:44.769
I´m sure you couldn´t.

00:08:44.769 --> 00:08:53.580
But, you could easily name 5 or 10 American
enterprises created in the last decade.

00:08:53.580 --> 00:09:01.410
“Immigrant founders started 52 percent of
all new Silicon Valley companies between 1995

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.560
and 2005”

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:08.370
The entrepreneurial rate among the immigrant
populations is between two and three times

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:09.550
higher than natives.

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:12.870
And this is a trend you find in every country.

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:17.050
For instance, one of the founders of Google,
Sergey Brinn, was born in Moscow.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:22.180
The co-founder of Whatsapp, Jan Coum, is Ukrainian.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:26.690
But it’s not just about Silicon Valley start
ups.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:30.959
Just have a walk in your neighbourhood and
you will see hundreds of Chinese stores, Mexican

00:09:30.959 --> 00:09:35.440
restaurants, and all kinds of small businesses
created by immigrants

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.960
It makes complete sense that immigrants will
have an entrepreneurial spirit.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:43.810
At the end of the day, those who leave their
country are natural risk takers.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:48.880
Not only that, but immigrants brings another
culture with them which makes it easier for

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.570
them to think outside of the box.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:57.750
Let’s look at an example: Charles Ferlmant
was a German immigrant who arrived to New

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.579
York City in the 19th century.

00:09:59.579 --> 00:10:03.810
Soon he realized the workers in the city needed
some kind of food that could be easily cooked

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:05.350
and sold on the street.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:09.800
That’s when he decided to import sausages
from his home country - this is how the HOT

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:10.860
DOG was born.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:14.830
Today, this meal feeds millions of people
around the planet.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:20.820
And this is just one example, there are thousands
of stories like this.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:25.290
In short, when cultures mix, new ideas and
new methodologies are created.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:28.500
This is what businesspeople call INNOVATION.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:33.940
And this is the special sauce that makes companies
and countries grow.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:38.180
So What´s going on in Japan?

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:42.790
Unsurprisingly, the have the lowest entrepreneurial
rate in the Industrialized world.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:45.800
Just 7% of their population decides to start
a company.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:49.920
By comparison, in Canada or New Zealand, this
percentage is 10%.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.250
The Japanese dream is not to start a business,
but to get hired by one that already exists.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:11:00.259
You know, those big companies like SONY or
TOSHIBA, those companies that have same corporate

00:11:00.259 --> 00:11:04.940
structure and the same work culture that they
had in the eighties.

00:11:04.940 --> 00:11:12.370
“Traditional Japanese electronics powerhouses
such as Sharp and Sony have incurred huge

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:19.189
losses and shed thousands of jobs, while competitors
Apple and Samsung have continued to increase

00:11:19.189 --> 00:11:20.610
their market shares.”

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:25.670
Those who like football/soccer might keep
up with the UEFA and the World Cup.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:30.189
Twenty years ago, there were at least two
Japanese companies sponsoring this events.

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:35.029
In 2016, the European Cup had zero Japanese
sponsors.

00:11:35.029 --> 00:11:40.639
No matter where you look Japanese firms are
struggling to compete with European, American

00:11:40.639 --> 00:11:42.279
and even Chinese companies.

00:11:42.279 --> 00:11:45.639
And the reason is not a lack of money but
a lack of innovation.

00:11:45.639 --> 00:11:53.459
This explains why Japan’s economy have been
frozen for two decades.

00:11:53.459 --> 00:11:59.339
And of course, this has an impact on the daily
life of it’s citizens.

00:11:59.339 --> 00:12:03.040
In order to keep a high level of productivity,
Japanese workers have the longest working

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.629
hours and the shortest vacations in all the
OECD countries.

00:12:06.629 --> 00:12:12.630
And, meanwhile, they have the same salary
that their parents had.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:17.329
So now we want to hear your opinion.

00:12:17.329 --> 00:12:19.920
Do you think Japan should open their doors
to immigrants?

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.640
Or do you still think immigration is a problem
that needs to be stopped?

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.639
You can leave your response in the comments!

